118: +#  dev_vme.c's default: ended the emulator (exit(1), announced only by debug() -- silent while
119: +#  free-running) on any VME2 offset the switch did not name.  Now: the 26 header-named registers
120: +#  the model does not implement DECLINE (reads served the preloaded word, writes dropped, one
121: +#  latched fatal() per register); every other unmatched offset returns 0, and for a guest data load
122: +#  or store memory_rw raises the m88k data-access exception.  The rung-3 witness
123: +#  (regress/artifacts/vmedefaultkill/witness_20261020/, 7 of 7 guest sites rc 1 on 5dbc000e) is NOT
124: +#  run here; this is its detector.  Needs only the binary: the probe constructs mvme88k/mvme187 with
125: +#  -M 64 and a 4-byte dummy image at 0x10000 -- no PROM image.  Kill tables:
126: +#  regress/artifacts/vmedefaultkill/killtable1_20261020/ (rev 2) and killtable2_20261021/ (rev 3).
127: +VMEDLOG=$LOGDIR/vme_default.log
