641: +# `#568` (vmedefaultkill): the MVME187's VME2 controller model ended the emulator on any offset its switch did not name -- the 26 header-named registers it does not implement now DECLINE with one announce per register, every other unmatched offset FAULTS to the guest; with a 38-row rung-3 detector, gated in gate 14
642: +
643: +**The defect** (`vmedefaultkill`, HIGH).  `DEVICE_ACCESS(vme)` named ten offsets of its 4 KiB window; every other offset
644: +reached `default:`, which printed with `debug()` -- silent at default verbosity while free-running -- and called
645: +`exit(1)`, so the emulator ended with no visible reason.  The device exists only on `-E mvme88k -e mvme187` (window
646: +0xfff40000-0xfff40fff).  The OpenBSD 2.2 mvme88k driver's attach reads MASTERCTL and writes MASTERCTL, MASTER3, MASTER4
647: +and MASTER4MOD -- four of the unimplemented registers -- so on HEAD that guest's attach would end the emulator at its
648: +first MASTERCTL read (read from the driver source; the witness measures the access sites, not a boot).  Witness, rung 3
649: +on unmodified `-E mvme88k -e mvme187` at HEAD 5dbc000e: 7 of 7 guest access sites end the emulator (rc 1), and a
650: +free-running MASTERCTL read dies with no `[ vme:` text (`regress/artifacts/vmedefaultkill/witness_20261020/SUMMARY.md`).
651: +
652: +**The rulings it implements.**  Owner, 2026-09-11: population 1 (word starts the header does not name, and every
653: +sub-word start) FAULTS -- `return 0`, which `memory_rw.c` turns into the m88k data-access exception for a guest data
654: +load or store.  Owner, 2026-10-09: population 2 (the 26 header-named registers with no case) DECLINE + ANNOUNCE ONCE --
655: +reads served the preloaded word, writes dropped, one latched `fatal()` per register, `(once)`, `#501`'s shape.
656: +
657: +**What ships.**
658: +* `src/devices/dev_vme.c` -- 26 exact case labels (SADDR2 .. MISC) decline: a read is served `d->reg[]`'s word, which
659: +  is 0 because nothing writes those words (odata is deliberately not forced to 0, so a store a later edit added would
660: +  show in a read-back); a write is dropped; a new `uint64_t warned_unimpl` latch (one bit per register word,
661: +  `relative_addr >> 2`, the highest 35) prints one `[ vme: unimplemented read from register 0x%x (len %d) -- served
662: +  0x%llx.  (once) ]` or `... write to register 0x%x (len %d): 0x%llx -- declined.  (once) ]` per register per device,
663: +  the first access's direction deciding the wording.  A compile-time check makes a field narrower than 36 bits an
664: +  error (the `1ULL` in the shifts is NOT checked there; the probe's announce rows catch a narrowed literal at run time
665: +  -- measured, leg M_ONENARROW).  `default:` keeps both `debug()` lines and returns 0 instead of `exit(1)`.  `est/`
666: +  byte-identical; `build/`, `build-asan/` and `/tmp/gxsec-build` rebuilt and cleared both parts.
667: +* `regress/vme_default_probe.py` (new, 38 rows, rev 3) -- controls (a bogus subtype, the session, a liveness `or`, the
668: +  DEVINIT VBR seed as the device signature, the free-running proof); the ten cased offsets read and their write paths
669: +  round-tripped; the 26 population-2 registers read and written (all 0, nothing stored, no fault) at word, sub-word
670: +  and doubleword widths; the announce in two free-running two-pass sessions covering 26 labels x {read, write} x
671: +  {latch clear, set}; the non-word first accesses and their second pass in the same process; a first-access ZERO store
672: +  (`p2 zero wr`); population-1 faults at the edges, an interior sample, both directions, all 988 word starts free-running,
673: +  eight widths and lanes, and no host text (`p1 quiet`); the interim sub-word pins `vmewidthlanes` will re-derive.
674: +  CONTROL rows are prerequisites, not causes: a CONTROL=FAIL says a prerequisite failed.  Its CONTRACT and NOT CLAIMED
675: +  list are its header; the store-data disclosure names its untested slice.  The shipped file differs from the copy kill
676: +  table 2 ran (`killtable2_20261021/vme_default_probe.rev3.frozen.py`) in docstring and comment text only -- the
677: +  repair-diff pass's records corrections; AST-identical with the docstring removed.
678: +* `regress/gate_arm.sh` (gate 14) -- the probe's block after `#536`'s mk48 block: completion sentinel, `vme_default rows
679: +  run` pinned at 38 (the score-claims pin), CONTROL `OK`, every row by name green exactly once, emitted/green/red pinned
680: +  at 38/38/0.
681: +* `regress/gate_hygiene.sh` (gate 6) -- by `tools/derive_hygiene_pins.sh`, never by hand: the probe GRANDFATHERED by name
682: +  (`--grandfather`) and `EXPECT_PTY_PROBES` 76 -> 77 (`--write`).  The census counts what lies in the tree the weekly
683: +  battery runs (the 2026-09-23 owner ruling), so 77 = 75 committed + this probe + another session's untracked
684: +  `lca_isaphys_probe.py`.  The probe is not promptless in substance -- its pty driver waits for `GXemul> ` with `in` and
685: +  `find` -- but the census keys on a code-level call of the ends-with method and cannot see that, as with
686: +  `alpha_tbi_probe.py`; the block note says so.
687: +* `tools/precommit_check.sh` -- `SCORE_CLAIMS_MANIFEST` 36 -> 37 (`vme_default rows run ... 38`).
688: +* `tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py` -- the probe's MANIFEST line (DETECTOR), the witness's two scripts (WITNESS)
689: +  and the tables' instruments and frozen copies (RESEARCH, by the `#471` definition at `CLASS_RESEARCH`).
690: +* `tools/pipeline/ledger.json` -- `vmedefaultkill` HELD for Fable 5.1's regress review (FABLE-ONLY; its question in
691: +  `hold_question`), with the pass-2, F2 and repair-pass seat entries and the not-fired seats named per phase (the five
692: +  pass-1 not-fired entries now carry the non-answer token); `vmewidthlanes` widened; `vmewarnedbit`, `vmeprobedebt` and
693: +  `m88kpsrmxm` filed.  `matrix.html` and `fable_queue.md` re-rendered.
694: +
695: +**Measured** (`regress/artifacts/vmedefaultkill/`; every MUTANT leg's prediction written first, in a `PRETABLE*` file
696: +whose mtime is the order proof -- table 2's three reference runs and the object comparison were built before PRETABLE2,
697: +which its section 0 discloses).
698: +* Kill table 1 (`killtable1_20261020/`, rev 2, 34 rows, fix568): 24 legs -- every one red except the two predicted
699: +  equivalents M_ODATA0 and M_SERVED0 (34/34: no population-2 word is ever non-zero); HEAD 14/34; clause (b) M_EXIT
700: +  24/34; clause (c): measured at `killtable1_20261020/legs/NULL.raw` (the vme `device_add` removed) 5/34 CONTROL=FAIL;
701: +  M_CAPNARROW fails to compile.  Eleven prediction misses, every one an incomplete prediction list
702: +  (`KILLTABLE1_VS_PRETABLE.out`).  Table 1b (`table1b/`): the three legs observation (c) owed, all red as predicted.
703: +* Pass 2's floor breach, measured BEFORE the repair (`killtable1_20261020/idata/`): M_IDATA -- the population-2 arm's
704: +  `if (writeflag == MEM_WRITE)` read as `if (idata)` -- 34/34 on the frozen rev 2, because every population-2 store the
705: +  probe made was non-zero.
706: +* Kill table 2 (`killtable2_20261021/`, rev 3, 38 rows, fix568b): 34 legs (27 regenerated, 7 new) -- 32 killed
707: +  (M_CAPNARROW by its failed build), the same 2 predicted survivors; M_IDATA red at `p2 zero wr` 0/1; one prediction
708: +  miss, M_ONENARROW, killed by four rows instead of two because GCC 15.2.1 -O3 folded the undefined `1u << 35` to 0 at
709: +  MISC (`obj/M_ONENARROW_codegen.txt`); BASE 38/38, HEAD 14/38, NULL 5/38 CONTROL=FAIL; no timeout red.  Its summary's
710: +  "first build log 01:16:55" is configure's (the first build is 01:17:37); a correction is appended to the file.

