786: @@ -25139,3 +25139,36 @@ Fable 5.1, GPT-6 Astra, Grok 4.7).  Each row's ledger `state_note` carries its s
787:    measurement.
788:  * **`ppcrldiclbanner` (LOW, open)** -- its first two items done (docstring line 2 and the first banner read DETECTOR; the
789:    usage message names `ppc_rldicl_probe.py`); open for the third, `vacuous cell`'s note split across two rows.
790: +
791: +
792: +### 2026-10-21 -- `vmedefaultkill` fixed by `#568`; `vmewidthlanes` widened; three rows filed
793: +
794: +* **`vmedefaultkill` (HIGH) -- FIXED by `#568`.**  `dev_vme.c`'s `default:` no longer ends the emulator: the 26
795: +  header-named VME2 registers the model does not implement DECLINE with one latched announce per register (owner
796: +  2026-10-09), and every other unmatched offset returns 0, which `memory_rw.c` turns into the m88k data-access exception
797: +  for a guest data load or store (owner 2026-09-11).  Rung-3 witness `regress/artifacts/vmedefaultkill/witness_20261020/`
798: +  (7 of 7 guest access sites rc 1 on HEAD 5dbc000e); detector `regress/vme_default_probe.py` (38 rows), gated in gate 14
799: +  and pinned at 38; kill table 2 and its addenda 2b/2c in `regress/artifacts/vmedefaultkill/killtable2_20261021/`; the
800: +  repair chain closed on the repair-diff pass (`r1_20261021/`).
801: +* **`vmewidthlanes` (LOW, open)** -- widened: population-2 SUB-WORD starts (the probe pins three interims --
802: +  `p3 interim`, `p2 int byte`, `p2 int half` -- that this row will re-derive) and cased-word `ld.d`/`st.d` lane
803: +  placement (a 32-bit register served into, or stored from, the wrong half of an 8-byte access at 0x00, 0x60, 0x88).
804: +* **`vmewarnedbit` (LOW, open)** -- new.  `dev_vme.c` writes its latch index `1ULL << (relative_addr >> 2)` twice, in
805: +  the test and in the set; one shared macro (`dev_pcc2.c`'s shape) would make a one-sided index edit impossible and a
806: +  two-sided relabel one edit.  D5 of `#568`'s pass-2 adjudication, filed rather than built: kill table 2 reds the
807: +  one-sided index edits it built (M_LATCHONE, M_ONENARROW), and the two-sided relabels the repair-diff pass named
808: +  (`1ULL` -> `2ULL`, `(relative_addr >> 2) ^ 1`) are equivalents.
809: +* **`vmeprobedebt` (LOW, open)** -- new.  Three rows of `regress/vme_default_probe.py` carry no own-channel kill in kill
810: +  table 2: `free quiet` (no leg reds it), `vbr rt` and `t1count inc` (red only as dependents of M_DROPTCTL).  The absent
811: +  legs: a cased arm's `debug()` -> `fatal()` promotion; a VBR write-path break; a T1COUNT write-path break.  Also the
812: +  clause-(e) cells the probe's NOT CLAIMED list names: the store-data slice (28 of 64 bits clear in every store value;
813: +  bit 1 measured 38/38 in table 2b), the latch set skipped for a zero store (M_ZEROSET, 38/38 in table 2d: the sampled
814: +  zero pins the announce's form, not the set), and `default:` serving 0xffd..0xfff (M_DFLTFFC, 38/38).  Coverage debt,
815: +  ranked below live defects.
816: +* **`m88kpsrmxm` (MED, open)** -- new.  A guest that sets PSR.MXM STOPS THE EMULATED CPU: `src/cpus/cpu_m88k.c`'s PSR
817: +  write prints `stcr: TODO: MXM support` at ERROR level and sets `cpu->running = false` (the `M88K_PSR_MXM` arm of the
818: +  control-register store).  The MC88100 manual (`_scratchpad/mc88100.txt:2047-2052`, `:9243-9245`) makes MXM the
819: +  misaligned-access exception MASK: when set, a misaligned access does not trap and the processor rounds the address
820: +  down to a consistent boundary.  Named on `#568`'s pass 1 (Fable) as an unmodelled divergence and adjudicated FILE,
821: +  LOW, before anyone read the arm; the arm halts, so it is filed MED.  Whether an in-tree guest sets MXM is not
822: +  established -- the reachability question that ranks it.
