regress/artifacts/fablequeue7n_20261009/fable5_rule7n_4.md:107:**ELSE #4 -- "FAULT is available on M88K" is true of DELIVERY and silent about RECOVERY.** The emulator sets DMT0/DMD0/DMA0 on DATA_ACCESS (`cpu_m88k.c:908-917`) and models no DPFSR at all (grep -ri over `src/cpus`, `src/include`: nothing). OpenBSD 2.2's probe path needs no DPFSR (SR1 flag), so probes recover; its non-probe kernel path keys on DPFSR and `pcb_onfault` and cannot. The carrier's "CHECK IT IS AVAILABLE ON THIS CPU" caveat should read "...and check what the guest does with it outside a probe" -- for FAULT the second half is where this round's answer actually lived.

