## Q1 -- rulings (id | ruling | reason)

| id | ruling | reason |
|---|---|---|
| F1 | UPHOLD | In the (d) closure by clause (2): `idata` is read by the write-form `fatal()` the direction predicate guards. Re-checked every population-2 store in the working probe: `p2 ann wr` / `p2 wr census` store r2 = 0xa5a5a5a5, the nw session stores r12 (0xd4 / 0xc3d4) and r10:r11 (0x1122334455667788), `p2 st widths` the same seeds; no zero store anywhere; reads leave idata 0. 34/34 is the right prediction, and measuring the FROZEN rev-2 instrument before building a row is the right order. |
| F2 (mine) | UPHOLD finding; REFINE fix | Reword + delete the always-true `sizeof(1ULL)` conjunct is right (no object-code footprint; the pcc2 precedent at dev_pcc2.c:181-182 has the same inert shape and never made the claim). But the D5 test is not decisive: M_ONENARROW's kill is UB-mediated. On x86-64 `1u << 35` masks to bit 3 = SLAVELMOD2's; in `p2 ann rd`'s order 0x0c is touched before 0x8c, so MISC is silenced -> 25/26 -> red. On a target whose 32-bit shift by >= 32 yields 0, MISC never latches -> `p2 ann rd 2` reds instead. A kill either way, by DIFFERENT rows, so "adopt the macro if it escapes" is a condition that cannot fire; write "macro FILED" outright and record the platform beside the leg. |
| F3 (mine) | OVERTURN the FIX (finding stands) | Guest source, re-read: `vme2chip_init()` runs at attach (vme.c:351, BUS_PCCTWO) and touches MASTERCTL (:452 read, :494 write-back), MASTER3 (:467), MASTER4 (:480), MASTER4MOD (:482) -- four registers; the `master1/master2` reads are `#if 0`. A struct-field grep of all of `sys/arch/mvme88k` for the 26 population-2 fields finds NO other site. IRQSTAT (:576) and IRQCLR (:581) live only in `vme2abort()`, installed as the ABORT-switch NMI handler by `intr_establish(110, &sc->sc_abih)` at :539 -- and dev_vme.c contains no interrupt assertion at all, so vector 110 is never delivered by this model. "Reaches five" (my pass-2 count, adopted by the packet) is an overcount for every boot the emulator can run. Wording: "has sites at six; attach reaches four (MASTERCTL, MASTER3, MASTER4, MASTER4MOD); vme2abort(), the ABORT-switch NMI handler, reads IRQSTAT and writes IRQCLR only on the abort bit -- this model raises no VME2 interrupt, so that path never runs here." |
| F4 | UPHOLD | memory_rw.c:620-622: `cache == CACHE_INSTRUCTION ? INSTRUCTION_ACCESS : DATA_ACCESS`; :584 and :603 keep `no_exceptions` callers out. Qualifier belongs in both the device and the gate comment. |
