2047: MXM - Misaligned Access Enable
2048:      This bit is set by software to disable the misaligned access exception. When this bit
2049:       is set and a misaligned access is attempted, the processor truncates the address to a
2050:      consistent boundary. See 6.5.2 Misaligned Access Exception for more information.
2051:         0- Misaligned Data Access Causes an Exception
2052:          1 - Misaligned Data Access Does Not Cause an Exception
2053: 
9243:  This exception can be masked by setting the MXM bit (bit 2) in the PSR. If this exception
9244:  is masked and a misaligned access is attempted, the processor rounds the address down
9245:  to a consistent boundary (for example, a half-word read operation attempted to address
9246:  $401 returns the half word at location $400).

